edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514238 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514238 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514238 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186513571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514238 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "27448a27-2ab1-5f66-ac78-eb27dc883118" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186513947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186514112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514336 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ea9559f3-a3c8-59ae-9017-a04ed616a025" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514400 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514400 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109877" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514400 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514400 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T}))=2,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514400 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5241b6a1-96aa-5720-ba1b-4d884df832da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514400 #edb/ref 1074 "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=3,$ $n=2,$ and $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) & =n-r=2-2=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514442 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514442 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109858" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514442 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514442 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ for all compatible matrices $A$ and $B?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A+B)$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A+B)$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514442 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9d632f6e-3556-5d97-834c-4e1de9c56681" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514442 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ is the row space of $({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})^{T}=A+B.$ This consists of all linear combinations of the rows of $A+B.$\n\nIf a vector is orthogonal to every linear combination of the rows of $A+B,$ it must be orthogonal to each row of $A+B.$\nBut notice that when pre-multiplying a vector by $A+B,$ we actually multiply each row of $A+B$ by that vector.\nSo, $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ must be orthogonal to the null space of $A+B,$ which is $\\text{Null}(A+B).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514490 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514490 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "14c1aa12-7e87-5b1e-9c66-6bd7f1359f4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514490 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514495 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514495 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2df8d215-4169-5ff0-96f8-b514b08b3eb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514495 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186362770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514504 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514504 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "56314e20-2366-500d-aee8-f1badacd2314" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514504 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186514442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514513 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186514528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514513 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "78d36b97-fb9f-562b-a664-3f90af4e59df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514513 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514528 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bc095201-9245-5703-95d0-69f9cc120dd7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514528 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186514400 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
